## Hard-won gotchas (real, from the 1.2.0 release)

- **asc credential storage:** the Windows keychain backend did **not** persist between shells.
  Use `asc auth login --bypass-keychain ...` so creds land in `~/.asc/config.json` (durable). The
  `.p8` itself is then embedded there with restricted perms — fine for a personal machine / CI.
- **"A required agreement is missing or has expired"** on every API call = an unsigned agreement in
  App Store Connect → Business (Agreements, Tax, and Banking). Only the Account Holder can accept it.
  After accepting, the API can lag a few minutes to propagate even when the UI shows "Active".
- **Submitting for review:** `asc` has no standalone submit-create command (`asc publish appstore
  --submit` re-uploads an IPA). For a build already uploaded via `eas submit`, submit via the
  reviewSubmissions API (create submission → add version item → PATCH `submitted:true`). This is
  baked into `scripts/release.ps1` step 7.
- **bun on this machine:** must be ≥1.3 for the text `bun.lock`; `bun install` sometimes leaves an
  incomplete `node_modules` (phantom expo-doctor failures) — `bun install --force` fixes it. EAS
  installs fresh in a clean container, so this only affects local verification.
- **expo-doctor before every build:** it caught 3 missing native deps (expo-font/blur/web-browser)
  that would have failed the cloud build. Run `npx expo-doctor` + `bunx tsc --noEmit` pre-release.
